      "reasoning": "Command responsibility arises when a superior knew or should have known about the commission of crimes by forces under his effective control and failed to take necessary measures to prevent them or punish the perpetrators. The commander directed the JNA military police to withdraw, leaving the prisoners in the hands of hostile Territorial Defence and paramilitary units who subsequently executed them. This omission satisfies the requisite knowledge and failure to act.",
